    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_91fd28b5",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent; overall-intent-description: The meme juxtaposes two images: the top image shows a group of people visibly grieving after a tragedy, with text labeling them as 'normal people after a tragedy.' The bottom image shows a man smiling while holding a coffee cup and looking at a laptop, with text reading 'me: oh man these memes are going to be fucking great.' The overall intent is to humorously contrast genuine emotional suffering with the cynical, detached amusement of someone anticipating the creation of memes from that tragedy. The meme's intent is to satirize the tendency of internet culture to commodify and trivialize real human suffering for entertainment. There is no toxicity present in the form of abusive, cyberbullying, harmful, hateful, misogynous, or propaganda content. The humor is derived from the absurdity of the contrast, not from targeting any specific group or individual based on protected characteristics. The intent is to highlight the irony and detachment of internet culture in the face of real tragedy, using analogical mapping: the image of genuine grief is mapped onto the text 'normal people after a tragedy,' while the image of the smiling man is mapped onto the text 'me: oh man these memes are going to be fucking great,' creating a juxtaposition that underscores the meme's satirical message.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_88e20c40"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
